Lab: Filter Data Using Jinja2 in Ansible
Objectives
By the end of this lab, students will be able to:

Understand the fundamentals of Jinja2 templating in Ansible
Apply built-in Jinja2 filters for string manipulation, list/dictionary processing, and data conversion
Build a Jinja2 template that generates a network device configuration file
Build a Jinja2 template that generates an application configuration file from the same source data
Verify generated output against the source variables to confirm the templating logic is correct
Prerequisites
Before starting this lab, students should have:

Basic understanding of Ansible playbooks and YAML syntax
Familiarity with Linux command line operations
Understanding of data types (strings, lists, dictionaries)
Previous exposure to Ansible variables and facts
This lab runs entirely against localhost, so no remote target hosts or SSH connectivity are required. All templates are rendered locally and written to a local output directory.

Install Ansible on your practice machine before starting:

python3 -m pip install --user ansible
ansible --version
You should see ansible [core X.Y.Z] or similar output confirming the installation succeeded.

Lab Environment
This lab uses a single control node (your practice machine) and runs all plays against localhost with connection: local. No inventory of remote hosts, SSH keys, or network access to other machines is needed. This keeps the lab fully self-contained and focused on Jinja2 templating logic rather than infrastructure setup.

Task 1: Explore Core Jinja2 Filters
Subtask 1.1: Set Up the Lab Directory Structure
Create a working directory and the source data file that every later task will reuse.

mkdir -p ~/ansible-jinja2-lab
cd ~/ansible-jinja2-lab
mkdir -p playbooks templates vars output

cat > ansible.cfg << 'EOF'
[defaults]
inventory = inventory.ini
host_key_checking = False
EOF

cat > inventory.ini << 'EOF'
[local]
localhost ansible_connection=local ansible_python_interpreter=auto_silent
EOF
Deliverable: the directory ~/ansible-jinja2-lab exists with playbooks/, templates/, vars/, output/, ansible.cfg, and inventory.ini. Confirm with ls -R ~/ansible-jinja2-lab.

Subtask 1.2: Create Sample Data Variables
This variable file is the single source of data used by every playbook and template in the lab.

cat > vars/sample_data.yml << 'EOF'
---
users:
  - name: john_doe
    email: john.doe@company.com
    department: engineering
    join_date: "2023-01-15"
    active: true
  - name: jane_smith
    email: jane.smith@company.com
    department: marketing
    join_date: "2022-11-20"
    active: false
  - name: bob_wilson
    email: bob.wilson@company.com
    department: sales
    join_date: "2023-03-10"
    active: true

network_config:
  domain: company.local
  dns_servers:
    - 8.8.8.8
    - 8.8.4.4
  vlans:
    - id: 10
      name: management
      subnet: 192.168.10.0/24
    - id: 20
      name: production
