Deliverable: vars/sample_data.yml is created. Validate it parses correctly:

ansible localhost -m debug -a "var=hostvars" -e "@vars/sample_data.yml" | head -n 5
You should see no YAML parsing errors in the output.

Subtask 1.3: Apply Basic String and List Filters
cat > playbooks/01-string-filters.yml << 'EOF'
---
- name: Demonstrate basic Jinja2 filters
  hosts: local
  gather_facts: false
  vars_files:
    - ../vars/sample_data.yml
  vars:
    sample_text: "  Hello World from Ansible  "
    mixed_case: "ThIs Is MiXeD cAsE tExT"

  tasks:
    - name: Display original strings
      debug:
        msg:
          - "Original text: '{{ sample_text }}'"
          - "Mixed case: '{{ mixed_case }}'"

    - name: Apply case and whitespace filters
      debug:
        msg:
          - "Uppercase: {{ sample_text | upper }}"
          - "Lowercase: {{ mixed_case | lower }}"
          - "Title case: {{ mixed_case | title }}"
          - "Trimmed: '{{ sample_text | trim }}'"
          - "Replaced: {{ sample_text | replace('World', 'Universe') }}"
          - "Length of trimmed text: {{ sample_text | trim | length }}"

    - name: Chain multiple filters together
      debug:
        msg: "Chained: {{ sample_text | trim | upper | replace('HELLO', 'GREETINGS') }}"

    - name: Extract and transform list data from users
      debug:
        msg:
          - "All user names: {{ users | map(attribute='name') | list }}"
          - "Active user names: {{ users | selectattr('active') | map(attribute='name') | list }}"
          - "Engineering users: {{ users | selectattr('department', 'equalto', 'engineering') | map(attribute='name') | list }}"
          - "Sorted VLAN IDs: {{ network_config.vlans | map(attribute='id') | list | sort }}"
EOF

ansible-playbook playbooks/01-string-filters.yml
Deliverable and expected result: the playbook completes with PLAY RECAP showing ok=4 and no failed tasks. The debug output for the last task must display Active user names: ["john_doe", "bob_wilson"] and Engineering users: ["john_doe"], confirming selectattr and map filtered the list correctly.

Task 2: Build Jinja2 Templates for Configuration Files
Subtask 2.1: Create a Network Device Configuration Template
cat > templates/router-config.j2 << 'EOF'
!
! Router Configuration Generated by Ansible
! Generated on: {{ ansible_date_time.iso8601 }}
! Template version: {{ app_settings.version }}
!
hostname {{ inventory_hostname | upper }}
!
ip domain-name {{ network_config.domain }}
{% for dns in network_config.dns_servers %}
ip name-server {{ dns }}
{% endfor %}
!
{% for vlan in network_config.vlans %}
vlan {{ vlan.id }}
 name {{ vlan.name | upper }}
!
{% endfor %}
!
{% if app_settings.debug_mode %}
logging console debugging
{% else %}
logging console warnings
{% endif %}
!
line vty 0 {{ app_settings.max_connections - 1 }}
 exec-timeout {{ app_settings.timeout }} 0
 transport input ssh
!
{% for user in users %}
{% if user.active %}
! User: {{ user.name | title }} ({{ user.department | title }})
! Email: {{ user.email }}
username {{ user.name | upper }} privilege 15
{% endif %}
{% endfor %}
!
end
EOF
Deliverable: templates/router-config.j2 exists and contains {% for %} / {% if %} blocks that reference network_config, app_settings, and users.

Subtask 2.2: Create an Application Configuration Template
cat > templates/app-config.j2 << 'EOF'
# Application Configuration File
# Generated by Ansible on {{ ansible_date_time.iso8601 }}
# Host: {{ inventory_hostname }}
# Environment: {{ app_settings.environment | upper }}

[application]
version = {{ app_settings.version }}
environment = {{ app_settings.environment }}
debug = {{ app_settings.debug_mode | lower }}
max_connections = {{ app_settings.max_connections }}
timeout = {{ app_settings.timeout }}

[network]
domain = {{ network_config.domain }}
{% for dns in network_config.dns_servers %}
dns_server_{{ loop.index }} = {{ dns }}
{% endfor %}

{% for vlan in network_config.vlans %}
vlan_{{ vlan.name }}_id = {{ vlan.id }}
vlan_{{ vlan.name }}_subnet = {{ vlan.subnet }}
{% endfor %}

[security]
{% if app_settings.environment == 'production' %}
ssl_required = true
session_timeout = {{ app_settings.timeout * 60 }}
{% else %}
ssl_required = false
session_timeout = {{ app_settings.timeout * 120 }}
{% endif %}

{% for user in users %}
{% if user.active %}
user_{{ user.name }}_level = {% if user.department == 'engineering' %}admin{% else %}user{% endif %}

user_{{ user.name }}_email = {{ user.email }}
{% endif %}
{% endfor %}

[summary]
total_users = {{ users | length }}
active_users = {{ users | selectattr('active') | list | length }}
admin_users = {{ users | selectattr('department', 'equalto', 'engineering') | selectattr('active') | list | length }}
total_vlans = {{ network_config.vlans | length }}
config_generated = {{ ansible_date_time.iso8601 }}
EOF
Deliverable: templates/app-config.j2 exists with an [application], [network], [security], and [summary] section, using loops and conditionals to generate content from sample_data.yml.

Task 3: Render Templates and Verify Output
Subtask 3.1: Create the Master Configuration Generator Playbook
cat > playbooks/02-master-config-generator.yml << 'EOF'
---
- name: Master configuration generator
  hosts: local
  gather_facts: true
  vars_files:
    - ../vars/sample_data.yml

  tasks:
    - name: Create output directories
      file:
        path: "{{ playbook_dir }}/../output/{{ item }}"
        state: directory
      loop:
        - network-configs
        - app-configs

    - name: Generate router configuration
      template:
        src: ../templates/router-config.j2
        dest: "{{ playbook_dir }}/../output/network-configs/{{ inventory_hostname }}-router.cfg"

    - name: Generate application configuration
      template:
        src: ../templates/app-config.j2
        dest: "{{ playbook_dir }}/../output/app-configs/{{ inventory_hostname }}-app.cfg"

    - name: Display confirmation message
      debug:
        msg: "Configuration files generated under {{ playbook_dir }}/../output/"
EOF
Deliverable: playbooks/02-master-config-generator.yml is a complete, syntactically valid playbook. Confirm with:

ansible-playbook --syntax-check playbooks/02-master-config-generator.yml
Expected output: playbook: playbooks/02-master-config-generator.yml with no syntax errors reported.

Subtask 3.2: Run the Playbook and Inspect Generated Files
ansible-playbook playbooks/02-master-config-generator.yml
Expected result: PLAY RECAP shows localhost with ok=4 changed=3 unreachable=0 failed=0.

Now inspect the generated files:

cat output/network-configs/localhost-router.cfg
cat output/app-configs/localhost-app.cfg
Subtask 3.3: Verify Correctness Against Source Data
Confirm the rendered files match the logic defined in the templates and source variables.

grep "hostname LOCALHOST" output/network-configs/localhost-router.cfg
grep "username JOHN_DOE" output/network-configs/localhost-router.cfg
grep -c "username" output/network-configs/localhost-router.cfg

grep "environment = production" output/app-configs/localhost-app.cfg
grep "ssl_required = true" output/app-configs/localhost-app.cfg
grep "total_users = 3" output/app-configs/localhost-app.cfg
grep "active_users = 2" output/app-configs/localhost-app.cfg
grep "admin_users = 1" output/app-configs/localhost-app.cfg
Deliverable and expected result:

output/network-configs/localhost-router.cfg contains hostname LOCALHOST and exactly two username lines (JOHN_DOE and BOB_WILSON), since jane_smith has active: false and is excluded by the {% if user.active %} conditional.
output/app-configs/localhost-app.cfg contains total_users = 3, active_users = 2, and admin_users = 1, matching the counts computed by selectattr filters over vars/sample_data.yml.
ssl_required = true appears because app_settings.environment is production, confirming the conditional block in the template evaluated correctly.
Expected Outcomes
Two working Jinja2 templates (router-config.j2 and app-config.j2) that generate configuration files from a shared set of Ansible variables
A working playbook that renders both templates to output/network-configs/ and output/app-configs/ without errors
The ability to trace a value in the generated output back to the specific filter, loop, or conditional in the template that produced it
Troubleshooting
Symptom: template error while templating string: expected token 'end of print statement'. This usually means a Jinja2 expression is missing a closing }} or a filter argument has mismatched quotes. Check the exact line number reported in the error and count the curly braces on that line.
Symptom: generated .cfg file is missing expected username or vlan lines. This indicates the {% for %} or {% if %} block closed too early or a selectattr/equalto condition does not match the actual value in vars/sample_data.yml (check for case sensitivity, such as active: true versus the string "true").
Conclusion
In this lab you built and rendered two Jinja2 templates in Ansible, a network device configuration and an application configuration file, both driven from a single shared variables file. You practiced core Jinja2 filters such as upper, trim, selectattr, and map, and used loops and conditionals to control what content appears in the generated output based on data values like active status and environment. By running ansible-playbook --syntax-check before execution and then using grep to confirm specific lines and counts in the rendered files, you verified that the templating logic produced exactly the output the source data implied, which is the core skill needed to debug and trust Jinja2-driven configuration generation in real Ansible projects.
